-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.6 (2026-10-18, staged)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Recognize lc1 build-time manifests and skip client rendering of marked packages
  * Keep build-time conffile baselines separate from reversible local projections
  * Verify build-time payloads, fetch exact HR companions and resolve their locations
  * Build marked packages before checksums; require payload and HR proof at publication
  * Verify pre-squashfs projections and bind release ISO evidence to final artifact hashes
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.5 (2026-10-17)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * A dpkg started while another one runs calls pre-invoke, stops at dpkg's
    lock and never calls post-invoke; its pre-invoke replaced the list of
    restored conffiles with an empty one, so the running dpkg's post-invoke
    left them in their package's bytes: the list is now added to, never replaced
  * Every dpkg run projects again any recorded conffile found in its package's
    bytes, whatever list it is on; --project does the same for any file
  * verify says RESTORED for a file in its package's own bytes (not projected,
    not a problem), never "changed by the person"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.4 (2026-10-17)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * An upgrade of dpkg-stereo no longer projects every installed package again:
    the first projection runs on a first install, or after a removal
  * A file that comes back in bytes already projected and checked (a reinstall,
    or a file an upgrade did not change) is rendered again without a second check
  * A package dpkg rewrote in the same second its record was written is looked
    at again by the next dpkg run
  * --restore and --verify --deep read each package's .deb once, not once per file
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.3 (2026-10-17)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Records kept per package: a dpkg run reads and writes only what it touched
  * One guarded bash per projecting process for the shell checks
  * A few files are projected in-process, without a worker pool
  * Records of 0.1.1 and 0.1.2 are moved over at the first run
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.2 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * One acorn process per projecting process: QML and JavaScript checks 70x faster
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.1 (2026-10-16)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * MIT licence (Daniel's decision)
  * After dpkg, only packages it changed and conffiles restored for it are read
  * Files changed since their package installed them are left alone
  * Slimmer records; the build's reasons stay out of the image
  * verify: package versions, pristine conffiles, --deep against the .debs
